<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44784" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔπιστ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πίστις</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>trustworthy, trusty</i>, of persons, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.2.12
			</span></i> (
				Sup.
			); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῆμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>BCH</u>
					37.124
				</span></i>
			 (Abdera, <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔπιστα</span>
			<i>things easy to believe</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				151
			</span></i> (anap., 
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔπειστα</span>
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>easily believing, credulous</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				380
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1389a18
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐπίστως, ἔχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Th.</u>
					105
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>readily obeying</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Euc.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				3.6.63
			</span></i> (sed leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔπειστος</span>).</div>
